      "text": "The review record identifies a PZT-gated RNiO3/LSMO composite channel as the central contribution: interfacial charge-transfer and screening design is used to raise room-temperature nonvolatile resistance switching beyond single-layer channels. The final paper reports a geometry-dependent maximum for LNO(2.5)/LSMO(2), with Delta R/Ron of 38,440% and Roff/Ron of 385.4. A focused conceptual concern remains over describing the ultrathin-nickelate devices as Mott transistors without direct evidence for the proposed Mott-insulating channel state and carrier-density-tuning mechanism."
